{"/api/discogs/artist/10359/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"10359","image":"https://i.discogs.com/6rZWnI0eJvORw6f2DgTK9DxO9DvmcJXEUUfGfTWvKdk/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTEwMzU5/LTE2MDE4MTk3NDYt/MzI2Ny5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/pKYpAS_vaklrUO_hHaqPgnodhmMdvqu9EFQOQBq3Zf8/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTEwMzU5/LTE2MDE4MTk3NDYt/MzI2Ny5qcGVn.jpeg","profile":"The Verve were an English rock band that formed in Wigan in 1990.\r\nCore members: Richard Ashcroft (vocals), Nick McCabe (guitar), Simon Jones (bass), and Peter Salisbury (drums). Simon Tong was added as second guitarist for the album \"Urban Hymns\" but not included in the group's 2008 reformation.\r\n\r\nGroup formed simply as Verve in 1991 (they became The Verve in 1994 after a dispute with the jazz label Verve).  Early material tended toward guitar-based soundscapes influenced by My Bloody Valentine, but they would later become a more conventional alt-rock group.\r\n\r\nIn April 1999 The Verve announced that they had mutually agreed to disband. 8 years later the original band reconciled their differences and reunited to record a new album and resume touring.\r\n","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:10359","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":4850,"name":"Richard Ashcroft"},{"active":true,"id":107124,"name":"Simon Jones"},{"active":true,"id":290457,"name":"Nick McCabe"},{"active":false,"id":317702,"name":"Simon Tong"},{"active":true,"id":354332,"name":"Peter Salisbury"}],"namevariations":["Verve","神韻合唱團"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/10359-The-Verve","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.facebook.com/theverve","https://twitter.com/genuineverve","http://www.last.fm/music/The+Verve","http://www.myspace.com/theverve","http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Verve"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/1309006/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"1309006","image":"","imageThumb":"","profile":"","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:1309006","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["ERAM"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/1309006-Eram","type":"artist","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/artist/13911/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"13911","image":"https://i.discogs.com/NIve9l72rCR_3tWG13In4TkzbVz95frSZecRLL0l97s/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:597/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTEzOTEx/LTE3ODY5MDg4MzYt/MjgyMy5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/G2r_2Yme_gK8JqItvlt78Rh2nK9AQuPYdlaSaV2eme4/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTEzOTEx/LTE3ODY5MDg4MzYt/MjgyMy5qcGVn.jpeg","profile":"British synthpop duo of [a=Annie Lennox] (b. December 25, 1954, Aberdeen, UK) and [a=David A. Stewart] (b. September 9, 1952, Sunderland, UK). They first recorded together as members of new wave band [a=The Catch (2)] who would change their name to [a291650] and enjoy two UK top ten hits in early 1980, but disband before the year was out. In 1981, Lennox and Stewart made their debut as Eurythmics, though they struggled to gain recognition at first, only breaking through with their sixth single Sweet Dreams (Are Made Of This). This was the turning point of their career. They continued to be one of the leading synth pop groups throughout the eighties. After a long period of solo activities in the early and mid-90s Eurythmics re-united for one album and charity world tour in 1999 and in 2004 for the release of extended, remastered and repacked editions of their previous albums and a second hits compilation. Eurythmics released one song (the B-side of Put A Little Love In Your Heart by Annie Lennox & [a=Al Green]) under the alias The Spheres Of Celestial Influence, a name considered before naming themselves Eurythmics. They chose that name referring to the Dalcroze [i]eurhythmics[/i] pedagogical exercise system that Lennox had encountered as a child, aka the Dalcroze method.\r\n\r\nNote: there are combined audio & video masters for [m=72601], [m=319205] and [m=72522].","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:13911","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":1196592,"name":"The Spheres Of Celestial Influence"}],"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":23825,"name":"Annie Lennox"},{"active":true,"id":72308,"name":"David A. Stewart"},{"active":false,"id":128624,"name":"Dean Garcia"},{"active":false,"id":232662,"name":"Olle Romo"},{"active":false,"id":285617,"name":"Roger Pomphrey"}],"namevariations":["DaEurythmics","Eurhythmics","Eurithmics","Euritmics","Euritmiscs","Eury Thmics","Eurythm!cs","Eurythmic","EurythmicIs","Eurythmᴉcs","Eurytmics","The Eurythmics","Vurythmics","Юритмикс","יוריתמיקס","ユーリズミックス","舞韻合唱團","유리드믹스","유리스믹스"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/13911-Eurythmics","type":"artist","urls":["https://www.eurythmics.com/","https://www.facebook.com/eurythmics/","https://www.instagram.com/eurythmicsmusic/","https://twitter.com/eurythmics","https://www.youtube.com/@Eurythmicstv","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eurythmics","https://www.allmusic.com/artist/eurythmics-mn0000206241"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/236212/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"236212","image":"https://i.discogs.com/gE81u2lkOlPwGo1sGuhjR1P8IZ8AR2mXyQmmo7wJC6M/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:506/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTIzNjIx/Mi0xNzE5OTc4Njg4/LTk2NDEuanBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/99qSAup3IirsCwV2tmfoQWWt0oz0OSn1hn-ekkGcLkw/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTIzNjIx/Mi0xNzE5OTc4Njg4/LTk2NDEuanBlZw.jpeg","profile":"American jazz-funk / soul-jazz saxophonist, born 12 December 1943, Buffalo, New York, USA, died 17 December 1999, New York, USA.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:236212","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":[{"active":true,"id":46992,"name":"The Blackout Allstars"},{"active":false,"id":89885,"name":"Urban Knights"},{"active":true,"id":437878,"name":"The Louisiana Gator Boys"},{"active":true,"id":924190,"name":"CTI All-Stars"},{"active":false,"id":1868740,"name":"David Matthews Orchestra"},{"active":true,"id":4499351,"name":"The Mean Machine (3)"},{"active":true,"id":4781744,"name":"The Mark III Trio"}],"members":null,"namevariations":["G. Washington","G. Washington Jnr.","G. Washington Jr","G. Washington Jr.","G. Washington, Jr.","G.Washington","G.Washington Jr.","G.Washington, Jr.","Gr. Washington","Groover Washington","Groover Washington JR","Groover Washington Jr","Groover Washington Jr.","Groover Washington, Jr.","Grover Wash Jr","Grover Washingon","Grover Washington","Grover Washington Jnr","Grover Washington Jnr.","Grover Washington Jr","Grover Washington Jr (For \"Dr. J\")","Grover Washington Jr.","Grover Washington Junior","Grover Washington, Jnr","Grover Washington, Jr","Grover Washington, Jr.-B.","Grover Washington,J.","Grower Washington","Jr. Grover Washington","Washington","Washington Jr.","Washington, Jr.","グローバー・ワシントン、Jr.","グローヴァー・ワシントンJr.","小格羅佛華盛頓"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/236212-Grover-Washington-Jr","type":"artist","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grover_Washington_Jr.","https://www.whosampled.com/Grover-Washington,-Jr./sampled/","","https://www.allmusic.com/artist/grover-washington-jr-mn0000944206","https://www.allaboutjazz.com/musicians/grover-washington-jr/","https://blackpast.org/african-american-history/grover-washington-1943-1999/","https://www.bluenote.com/artist/grover-washington-jr/","https://www.bmhof.org/Inductees-W/Grover-Washington-Jr.html","https://musicianguide.com/biographies/1608000614/Grover-Washington-Jr.html"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/37912/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"37912","image":"https://i.discogs.com/QRDtaHHvhjbvw8gUoAwXDAd3BxpziZuv9L-xqJ58bKQ/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:593/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTM3OTEy/LTE3ODgzODE1NTct/NzA0OC5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/nv_4k1Copv9dgA4nxqnLlgE0BU3WLM3SdoWMztiIOF4/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTM3OTEy/LTE3ODgzODE1NTct/NzA0OC5qcGVn.jpeg","profile":"Southern Rapper from Athens, Georgia. Born March 6, 1977, Bubba started off rhyming under the wing of Athens rap veteran [a=Duddy Ken], he later signed with Jermaine Dupri, but nothing came out of that, and his music came into the hands of [a=Timbaland], who signed Bubba to his label and re-released his debut 'Dark Days, Bright Nights'. Beat Club Records folded, and Bubba is currently a part of [a=Big Boi]'s Purple Ribbon imprint.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:37912","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":688651,"name":"Warren Anderson Mathis"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["Bubba","Bubba Mathis (Sparxxx)","Bubba Sparks","Bubba Sparkx","Bubba Sparkxx","Bubba Sparx","Bubba Sparxx"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/37912-Bubba-Sparxxx","type":"artist","urls":["https://soundcloud.com/bubba-sparxxx","https://twitter.com/TheRealBubbaK","https://www.instagram.com/bubbamathis/","https://www.facebook.com/TheRealBubbaK/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/3840/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"3840","image":"https://i.discogs.com/1rOFEc5UAgD22TTmUwBfBmyRCGM3vdM8ghTG-C2iQtU/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:446/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTM4NDAt/MTc2MTY5NDAxNy03/ODM0LnBuZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/CkRUgew74o1pI0PKrW0gKYbadjLazsdgonRYDNvn87o/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTM4NDAt/MTc2MTY5NDAxNy03/ODM0LnBuZw.jpeg","profile":"Electronic and alternative rock (modern rock) band from Oxfordshire, England (United Kingdom).\r\n\r\nThe name Radiohead comes from the [a=Talking Heads] song, \"Radio Head\", from the \"[url=http://www.discogs.com/Talking-Heads-True-Stories/master/39386]True Stories[/url]\" album.\r\n\r\nFormed by school friends in 1985, Radiohead did not release their first single until 1992's \"[r=767600]\". The cathartic \"[url=http://www.discogs.com/Radiohead-Creep/master/21481]Creep[/url]\", from the debut album \"[url=http://www.discogs.com/Radiohead-Pablo-Honey/master/13344]Pablo Honey[/url]\" (1993), became a worldwide hit as grunge music dominated radio airwaves.\r\n\r\nRadiohead were initially branded as a one-hit wonder abroad, but caught on at home in the UK with their second album, \"[url=http://www.discogs.com/Radiohead-The-Bends/master/17008]The Bends[/url]\" (1995), earning fans with their dense guitar atmospheres and front man [a=Thom Yorke]'s expressive singing. The album featured the hits \"[url=http://www.discogs.com/Radiohead-High-Dry-Planet-Telex/release/199387]High & Dry[/url]\", \"[r=1463625]\" and \"[url=http://www.discogs.com/Radiohead-Fake-Plastic-Trees/master/21526]Fake Plastic Trees[/url]\".\r\n\r\nThe band's third album, \"[url=http://www.discogs.com/Radiohead-OK-Computer/master/21491]OK Computer[/url]\" (1997), propelled them to greater attention. Popular both for its expansive sound and themes of modern alienation, the album has been acclaimed by critics as a landmark record of the 1990s, some critics go as far to consider it one of the best of all time. \"[url=http://www.discogs.com/Radiohead-Kid-A/master/21501]Kid A[/url]\" (2000) marked further evolution, containing influences from experimental electronic music.\r\n\r\n\"[url=http://www.discogs.com/Radiohead-Hail-To-The-Thief/master/16962]Hail To The Thief[/url]\" (2003) was seen as a conventional return to the guitar and piano-led rock sound. After fulfilling their contract with EMI, Radiohead released \"[url=http://www.discogs.com/Radiohead-In-Rainbows/master/21520]In Rainbows[/url]\" (2007) famously via a pay-what-you-want model. Their latest album,  \"[url=https://www.discogs.com/Radiohead-A-Moon-Shaped-Pool/master/998252]A Moon Shaped Pool[/url]\", was released in May 2016.\r\n \r\nRadiohead's original influences were cited as alternative rock and post-punk bands like [url=http://www.discogs.com/artist/Smiths,+The]The Smiths[/url], [a=Pixies], [a=Magazine], [a=Joy Division] and [a=Siouxsie & The Banshees], who Thom Yorke claims inspired him to become a performer, and [a=R.E.M.] (with lead singer of the band, Thom Yorke, referring to himself as an 'R.E.M. groupie').\r\n\r\nBand members:\r\nThom Yorke – vocals, guitar, piano, keyboards, laptop (1985–present)\r\nColin Greenwood – bass guitar (1985–present)\r\nEd O'Brien – guitar, effects, backing vocals (1985–1990, 1990–present)\r\nPhilip Selway – drums, percussion (1985–present)\r\nJonny Greenwood – guitar, keyboards, ondes Martenot, glockenspiel, laptop, orchestral arrangements (1988–present)\r\n\r\nCurrent live members:\r\nClive Deamer – drums, percussion (2011–present)\r\n\r\nFormer members:\r\nRasmus \"Raz\" Peterson – tenor saxophone, alto saxophone (1985–1989)\r\nLiz Cotton – alto saxophone (1988–1989)\r\nCharlotte Cotton – alto saxophone (1988–1989)\r\nNigel Powell – drums (1990)\r\n\r\nPrevious names:\r\nOn a Friday (1985–1990, 1990–1991)\r\nShindig (1990)","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:3840","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":449561,"name":"TV Feet"},{"id":840842,"name":"On A Friday"},{"id":1506477,"name":"Shindig (2)"}],"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":4854,"name":"Thom Yorke"},{"active":true,"id":152377,"name":"Jonny Greenwood"},{"active":true,"id":365781,"name":"Phil Selway"},{"active":true,"id":365785,"name":"Colin Greenwood"},{"active":true,"id":365794,"name":"Ed O'Brien"}],"namevariations":["Radio Head","Radiohead (Samples)","Radioheads","radiohead","レディオヘッド","收音機頭樂隊","电台司令","電台司㠳合唱團","電台司令","電台司令合唱團","래디오헤드"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/3840-Radiohead","type":"artist","urls":["https://www.radiohead.com/","https://radiohead.bandcamp.com/","https://bsky.app/profile/radiohead.wastehq.social","https://www.facebook.com/radiohead","https://www.instagram.com/radiohead","https://myspace.com/radiohead","https://www.progarchives.com/artist.asp?id=1492","https://twitter.com/radiohead","https://www.whosampled.com/Radiohead/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radiohead","https://www.youtube.com/user/radiohead","https://www.allmusic.com/artist/radiohead-mn0000326249"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/47109/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"47109","image":"https://i.discogs.com/QX4yPgXzz7GnIb-fNV_ysApXOJcGyUJMI6c_kxIm1Mo/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTQ3MTA5/LTE2MTExNTIzOTMt/OTM3Ny5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/UzFTcUhYkwVmsbOegRpAPeMApWm_jAWucASqbboV41A/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTQ3MTA5/LTE2MTExNTIzOTMt/OTM3Ny5qcGVn.jpeg","profile":"All-girl pop group from London, England. \r\nActive in the following years: 1994-2000, 2007-2008, 2012, 2018-2019.\r\n\r\n[b]Members:[/b]\r\nMelanie Brown (\"Scary Spice\")\r\nMelanie Jayne Chisholm (\"Sporty Spice\")\r\nEmma Bunton (\"Baby Spice\")\r\nGeri Halliwell (\"Ginger Spice\")\r\nVictoria Beckham, née Adams (\"Posh Spice\")","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:47109","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":38024,"name":"Victoria Beckham"},{"active":true,"id":43105,"name":"Emma Bunton"},{"active":true,"id":51163,"name":"Geri Halliwell"},{"active":true,"id":271578,"name":"Melanie Chisholm"},{"active":true,"id":874050,"name":"Melanie Brown"}],"namevariations":["Sice Girls","Space G","Space Girl","Space Girls","Spice","Spice Giris","Spice Girl","Spice Girl's","Spice Girsl","Spice Grils","Spice Gs","Spie Girls","Spire Girls","Spise Girls","Spyce Girls","The Spice Girls","スパイス・ガールズ","英国辣妹","辣妹","辣妹合唱团","辣妹合唱團"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/47109-Spice-Girls","type":"artist","urls":["https://thespicegirls.com/","https://www.facebook.com/spicegirls","https://x.com/spicegirls","https://www.instagram.com/spicegirls/","https://www.youtube.com/user/Spi